mira: Quick update 3 I've assembled a minimal TypeScript monorepo Next starter + tiny eval harness for new hires. goal: exercise SDK parity (browser vs server), auth rotation patterns, and a basic LangChain/LlamaIndex compare.
sam: love it. can you drop the wiring details for both environments? folks always get tripped up by SSR auth.
mira: server-side example (simple wrapper):

```ts
// packages/api/src/redwoodClient.ts
import { Redwood } from 'redwood-sdk'
export const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_API_KEY })
```

mira: browser uses a proxied route that injects ephemeral rotation tokens. keeps secrets off the client and shows recommended pattern.

```ts
// apps/web/src/pages/api/proxy.ts
export default async function handler(req, res) {
  // rotate token per-session, forward request to Redwood API
  const token = await rotateSessionToken(req.cookies.sid)
  const r = await fetch(process.env.RW_API_BASE + req.query.to, {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
  })
  res.status(r.status).send(await r.text())
}
```

jon: does the proxy cause any retry-on-401 loops? we previously saw double refresh attempts when both client and proxy retried.
mira: yep that was a bug with SDK v0.8's refresh middleware. monorepo pins v0.9 and I added a defensive guard in middleware to prevent recursive retries.

```ts
// packages/api/src/middleware/authGuard.ts
export function authGuard(req, res, next) {
  if (req.headers['x-retry-count'] && Number(req.headers['x-retry-count']) > 1) {
    return res.status(401).send('auth-failed')
  }
  next()
}
```

katie: please add that snippet to the onboarding doc. new hires copy-paste and then wonder why SSR on the demo fails if they use localStorage.
sam: big note: cookie vs localStorage. the starter intentionally uses httpOnly cookie for session id. add a short blurb: "Avoid localStorage for server-side auth flows; it won't be available during SSR." and a small diagram.

mira: eval harness: tiny script compares a local quantized Llama (on dev machine) vs hosted redwood model for a set of prompt templates in e2e/prompts.json. it's purposely minimal so CI can run it fast.

README snippet:

```bash
yarn workspace @redwood/eval run --prompts=e2e/prompts.json --target=hosted --retries=1
```

jon: does CI run the eval on PRs? last time we had intermittent hosted timeouts and it blocked merges.

ci-bot: added a lightweight eval job on PRs: 3 prompts, per-prompt timeout 25s, retries 1. will report diffs to the PR comment.

mira: to surface failures without masking flakiness, default retries=1 in harness. toggles available for maintainers.
sam: can we include a troubleshooting section in README with: auth rotation loops, SSR mismatch (cookie/localStorage), CI flake mitigation, and model timeout tuning? saves time during onboarding.

mira: yes. also adding a tiny animated gif demonstrating running the local Llama eval vs hosted and the CI job annotation. PR inbound with docs + one-line tests.
katie: once merged drop a link in #devex and pin to the new-hire checklist. include a short checklist: clone, env setup, run dev, run eval, open browser demo.

mira: will do. thanks team :rocket:

